\section{Introduction}
Baduy (ISO 639-3 \texttt{bac}) is spoken by the Kanekes community in the mountains of western Java, Indonesia. It is conventionally treated as a Sundanese dialect but often considered a separate language. It has no official writing system. The 2015 census recorded 11,620 speakers according to Wikipedia.

\section{Primary Educational Resources}
None found in the searches.

\section{Linguistic and Reference Materials}
\begin{itemize}
\item Baduy language, Wikipedia. \url{https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Baduy_language}
\end{itemize}
No dictionary, glossary or grammar was found.

\section{Religious and Community Resources}
None found.

\section{Digital and Audio Resources}
\begin{itemize}
\item PARADISEC collection BAC01, ``Documenting the endangered Indonesian language of the Baduy Dalam''. \url{https://catalog.paradisec.org.au/repository/BAC01}
\item Research Data Australia record for the same documentation project. \url{https://researchdata.edu.au/documenting-endangered-indonesian-baduy-dalam/2369835}
\end{itemize}
Only the descriptions of these records were seen; their access conditions and contents were not checked.

\section{Curriculum Development Context}
There is little published material. The PARADISEC recordings may be the main documentation source, subject to the community's access conditions.

\end{document}
